On Saturday I play golf.

40
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,610
And on Sunday we play tennis.

41
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,040
When?

42
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,608
When do you play football?

43
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,490
On Monday!

44
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,728
When do you play basketball?

45
00:03:44,919 --> 00:03:46,523
On Tuesday!

46
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,481
When do you go roller-skating?

47
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,125
On Wednesday.

48
00:03:51,719 --> 00:03:53,687
When do you do your exercises?

49
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:55,244
On Thursday.

50
00:03:55,759 --> 00:03:57,567
When do you go swimming?

51
00:03:57,759 --> 00:03:59,204
On Friday.

52
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,368
When do you play golf?

53
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,050
On Saturday.

54
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,884
When do you play tennis?

55
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,570
On Sunday.

56
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,888
And it's Sunday today.

57
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,208
And we're playing tennis now.

58
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:18,049
Where's Princess Sylvia's room?

59
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,403
-There! -Where,

60
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,329
on the first floor?

61
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,961
No, it's on the second floor.

62
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:29,489
Oh, there are three rooms on the second floor.

63
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,809
Which one is it?

64
00:04:32,279 --> 00:04:35,362
-Is it the one on the left? -No, it isn't.

65
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,802
-Is it the one on the right? -No, it isn't.

66
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:43,002
-Is it the one in the middle? -Yes, it is.

67
00:04:43,519 --> 00:04:45,089
It's the one in the middle.

68
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,449
It's the one in the middle.

69
00:05:04,199 --> 00:05:06,566
What about the room up there?

70
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:09,360
The one on the top floor.

71
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:13,281
That's Corvax's room. It's the computer room.

72
00:05:55,959 --> 00:05:58,359
Stop it! Stop it!

73
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:01,608
No! No! No!

74
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:07,962
Food. Clocks. Seven p.m.

75
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:11,129
I've got some food.

76
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,930
I've got some clocks.

77
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,723
And it's nearly seven o'clock.

78
00:06:17,079 --> 00:06:18,284
OK.

79
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:22,690
Open the door... quietly!

80
00:06:24,959 --> 00:06:28,326
Look around... carefully!

81
00:06:29,839 --> 00:06:32,489
Run downstairs... quickly!

82
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,843
Hello Sylvia!

83
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,005
Hello.

84
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,446
That's me!

85
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,286
Oh!

86
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,401
It's seven. Bob's waiting.

87
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,650
That's me again!

88
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:00,523
Seven o'clock!

89
00:07:02,279 --> 00:07:04,168
It's dinner-time, Sylvia!

90
00:07:04,519 --> 00:07:07,090
-Yes, Mummy. -Yes, Mummy.

91
00:07:07,279 --> 00:07:09,646
-Yes, Mummy. -Yes, Mummy.

92
00:07:19,839 --> 00:07:23,968
Look, they're all Sylvias.

93
00:07:27,439 --> 00:07:30,010
How many are there?

94
00:07:31,879 --> 00:07:34,404
There are three in the kitchen.

95
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,523
Four in the hall.

96
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,768
There's one by the fireplace.

97
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:41,120
There are two against the wall.

98
00:07:41,879 --> 00:07:44,040
There's one in the sitting-room

99
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:46,004
bouncing on the chairs.

100
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:48,520
And four are having lots of fun,

101
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:50,563
sliding down the stairs.

102
00:07:51,319 --> 00:07:53,890
There are hundreds in the garden

103
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,684
picking all the flowers.

104
00:07:55,879 --> 00:07:58,450
And lots in the bathrooms

105
00:07:58,639 --> 00:08:00,800
turning on the showers.

106
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,561
Lots on the chandeliers.

107
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:05,567
More over there!

108
00:08:05,879 --> 00:08:09,803
More of them and more of them, appearing everywhere!

109
00:08:10,439 --> 00:08:14,363
More of them and more of them, appearing everywhere!

110
00:08:15,839 --> 00:08:18,682
Where are they all coming from?

111
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:21,922
Look,

112
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:25,647
they're coming from Corvax's room upstairs.

113
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:29,605
What's he doing? Go and see... quick!

114
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:32,440
Stop it! Stop it!

115
00:08:32,639 --> 00:08:33,969
Help!

116
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,651
Corvax!

117
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,245
What are you doing?

118
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:42,840
I'm not doing anything.

119
00:08:43,519 --> 00:08:45,248
It's the computer.

120
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:52,168
Help!

121
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,045
Listen!

122
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,570
Help!

123
00:08:55,759 --> 00:08:56,839
It's Sylvia.

124
00:08:59,639 --> 00:09:02,404
Oh, Bob! I'm frightened.

125
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,090
Why?

126
00:09:04,559 --> 00:09:05,924
Why are you frightened?

127
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:09,842
Because there are lots of Sylvias in the palace.

128
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:13,050
-Sylvias? -Excuse me.

129
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:16,730
Have you got any clocks?

130
00:09:16,919 --> 00:09:19,524
-Oh, Muzzy! -Here you are.

131
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:23,080
Muzzy, why do you eat clocks?

132
00:09:23,279 --> 00:09:25,929
Because I like them, of course.

133
00:09:34,559 --> 00:09:35,720
Why?

134
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:44,530
Oh, dear! He's crying.

135
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,089
Why are you crying?

136
00:09:48,279 --> 00:09:50,280
Because I can't reach the apple.

137
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:52,129
Why can't you reach the apple?

138
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,448
Because I'm small.

139
00:09:54,799 --> 00:09:56,164
I can reach the apple.

140
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,565
Yes.

141
00:09:57,799 --> 00:10:00,722
-Why? -Because you're tall.

142
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:01,965
Right!

143
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,441
-Here you are! -Thanks.

144
00:10:04,679 --> 00:10:06,009
Bye!

145
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:11,209
Hey! That's my apple, and my bike.

146
00:10:13,399 --> 00:10:15,685
Come back! Come back!

147
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,964
That's mine!

148
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,685
Gotcha!

149
00:10:21,879 --> 00:10:24,769
Now, is this my bike?

150
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:27,446
Yes, it's yours.

151
00:10:27,639 --> 00:10:29,447
Yes, it's mine.

152
00:10:30,039 --> 00:10:32,120
And where's my apple?

153
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,369
You can't have it.

154
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:37,402
-Why not? -Because it's in here.

155
00:10:38,879 --> 00:10:40,687
Oh, Bob.

156
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:44,406
Lots of Sylvias?

157
00:10:49,679 --> 00:10:52,888
Ah! I see.

158
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:57,367
Corvax! The computer!

159
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,286
Bob! Where are you going?

160
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:03,005
To the computer room. Come on!

161
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,440
Follow me!

